# Epicxstudios — creative technology guardrails

You are building the studio site for Epicxstudios: a K12 curriculum platform for state and CBSE syllabi, a training LMS for higher education and clinical programs, custom applications for training, and websites for education. The standard is a dark, precise, cinematic studio surface. Ship work that could sit in a design portfolio. Refuse generic SaaS layouts.

## Stack

- TypeScript only. Strict mode. No `any` unless a third-party type is genuinely unreachable, and then isolate it with a one-line comment.
- Next.js App Router under `src/app`. Server Components by default. Add `'use client'` only for motion, WebGL, or browser state.
- Tailwind CSS v4. Tokens live in `src/app/globals.css` inside `@theme`. Do not invent one-off hex values in components.
- Framer Motion (`framer-motion`) for cinematic transitions and micro-interactions. Import it from `"framer-motion"`.
- React Three Fiber for 3D. Canvas code lives in `src/components/canvas` and is loaded with `next/dynamic` and `ssr: false` from a client entry. Never import `three` into a Server Component.
- Springs live in `src/lib/motion.ts`. Use `uiSpring` for controls and `revealSpring` for entrances. Do not invent a new cubic-bezier for UI unless the moment is genuinely cinematic and documented.

## File placement

- `src/app/layout.tsx` — fonts, dark shell, skip link, navbar, footer.
- `src/app/page.tsx` — studio homepage. Keep it thin.
- `src/app/services/<track>/page.tsx` — one route per practice: `k12-education`, `training-lms`, `software-mobile`, `web-dev`.
- `src/components/Navbar.tsx` — the only primary navigation.
- `src/components/ui` — atomic controls (`Button`, `Panel`, `Reveal`). No barrel `index.ts` files.
- `src/components/canvas` — WebGL only.
- `src/lib/site.ts` — practice copy and routes. Change labels here so nav, footer, and pages stay in lockstep.

## Dark mode (required)

The site is dark-only. Do not add a theme toggle or a light theme.

| Token   | Hex       | Use                                      |
| ------- | --------- | ---------------------------------------- |
| ink     | `#07080d` | Page background                          |
| surface | `#12151c` | Panels                                   |
| ivory   | `#f4f0e6` | Primary text                             |
| muted   | `#a39c90` | Short secondary text                     |
| amber   | `#e7a23a` | Signal only: indexes, active marks, focus |
| ion     | `#8ee0cf` | Hairlines and instrument lines           |

- `<html>` sets `color-scheme: dark`. Body background is ink, body text is ivory.
- Amber is for labels, indexes, and focus. Never for paragraphs.
- Longer copy uses `text-ivory/75` or ivory, so it stays readable.
- Depth comes from a 1px `border-ivory/10`, backdrop blur, and a single warm radial glow. No heavy drop shadows. No purple, blue, or magenta gradients.
- Glass is reserved for the floating nav and sparse panels. Do not frost every section.

## Typography

- Display: Syne via `--font-display` (`font-display`). Tight tracking on large headlines (`tracking-tight` or about `-0.04em`).
- UI: Geist Sans (`font-sans`).
- Indexes and eyebrows: Geist Mono, uppercase, tracking about `0.28em`, size about 12px.
- Headlines are sentences with a point of view. Do not center every section. Left-align the editorial column; center only the floating nav cluster.
- One `h1` per page. Do not use divs as headings.

## Motion

- Every interactive control has a hover and a press state. Prefer `whileHover` / `whileTap` with scale between `0.98` and `1.03`, or a 1–2px translate on an arrow.
- The active nav item uses `layoutId` so the pill springs between links. Only one node with that id may be mounted.
- Entrances: `y: 18 → 0`, delayed in steps of `0.05–0.08s`, using `revealSpring`. Keep headline opacity at 1 so the first paint stays readable. Opacity fades are for menus and non-critical overlays. Run entrances once.
- Animate `transform` and `opacity`. Do not animate width, height, or top of large trees. Height animation is allowed only for the small mobile nav panel.
- Wrap the app in `MotionConfig` with `reducedMotion="user"`. Also honor `motion-reduce:` Tailwind variants for CSS transitions.
- Critical text must not depend on JavaScript to become visible. Reveal nodes carry `data-reveal`. Do not leave opacity at 0 when scripting is disabled.
- Page transitions stay quiet. Do not add full-screen wipes, parallax on body copy, or scroll-jacking.

## Layout

- Content column max width: `max-w-6xl`. Page padding: `px-5 md:px-8`.
- The nav is a floating pill, fixed, inset from the viewport, blurred ink at about 80% opacity. It is not a full-bleed admin bar.
- Mobile first. Below `md`, navigation collapses into a spring-opened panel. Hit targets are at least 44px. No horizontal page scroll.
- First viewport of the homepage is a full-bleed atmospheric scene with the headline in the lower third, sitting on a solid ink scrim. WebGL never sits on top of text.
- Repeating practice entries are editorial rows (index, title, summary, arrow), not a grid of equal icon cards.
- Sections need real vertical rhythm (`py-20` to `py-28`). Do not stack boxed cards with identical padding as a substitute for layout.

## 3D

- Decorative, pointer-reactive, and cheap. Cap particle counts near 80. Set `dpr={[1, 1.5]}`.
- `pointer-events` must leave links and buttons clickable. The canvas may receive the pointer only in empty space.
- No postprocessing, no heavy models, no continuous allocations inside `useFrame`.
- Dispose geometries created outside JSX. Pause or freeze the loop when the user prefers reduced motion.
- Mark decorative canvas wrappers `aria-hidden`.

## Accessibility and code

- Semantic regions: `header`, `nav`, `main`, `section`, `footer`. `main` has `id="content"` and the skip link targets it.
- Icon buttons need an accessible name. Menu buttons expose `aria-expanded` and `aria-controls`. Current links expose `aria-current="page"`.
- Visible focus: amber outline, 2px, offset. Do not remove outlines.
- Keyboard: Escape closes the mobile menu and returns focus to the menu button. Body scroll locks only while that menu is open.
- Internal navigation uses `next/link`. Do not use `<a>` for in-app routes.
- Props into client components must be serializable.
- Keep page files as composition plus `metadata`. Shared practice copy belongs in `src/lib/site.ts`.
- Do not add dependencies for a single widget. Prefer a small local component.
- No barrel re-exports. Import the module that defines the symbol.

## Voice and anti-patterns

Voice: precise, warm, concrete. Name the classroom, the device, the constraint. Avoid hype words (cutting-edge, unlock, elevate, seamless, next-gen, revolutionary).

Do not ship:

- Inter, Arial, or system fonts as the display face
- Purple-to-blue gradients, neon grids, or emoji used as icons
- Three identical feature cards with a lucide icon, a title, and a vague sentence
- A light mode, a hamburger that only toggles opacity, or a nav that is not usable at 320px
- Lorem ipsum, fake metrics, fake client logos, or an invented contact email
- `three` imported from a Server Component, or a canvas that blocks the headline

## Before finishing a UI change

Confirm all of the following:

1. Dark tokens only, from the theme.
2. Syne for display, mono for eyebrows, ivory text on ink.
3. Hover and press springs on new controls, with reduced motion covered.
4. The layout works at 320px and at desktop widths, with no overlap against the fixed nav.
5. Keyboard focus is visible and the new control has an accessible name.
6. WebGL, if added, is dynamic, decorative, and does not cover type.
